1
00:04:05,217 --> 00:04:11,217
The family just got a little stranger.

2
00:08:10,434 --> 00:08:16,434
Addams Family Values is a comedy, family, fantasy
film directed by Barry Sonnenfeld.

3
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:21,652
Siblings Wednesday and Pugsley Addams will stop at nothing to get rid of
Pubert, the new baby boy adored by parents Gomez and Morticia.

4
00:16:20,869 --> 00:16:26,869
Things go from bad to worse when the new "black widow" nanny, Debbie Jellinsky,
launches her plan to add Fester to her collection of dead husbands.

5
00:20:26,086 --> 00:20:32,086
Morticia Addams, played by Anjelica Huston.

6
00:24:31,304 --> 00:24:37,304
Gomez Addams, played by Raúl Juliá.

7
00:28:36,521 --> 00:28:42,521
Uncle Fester, played by Christopher Lloyd.

8
00:32:41,739 --> 00:32:47,739
Debbie Jellinsky, played by Joan Cusack.

9
00:36:46,956 --> 00:36:52,956
Wednesday Addams, played by Christina Ricci.

10
00:40:52,173 --> 00:40:58,173
Granny, played by Carol Kane.

11
00:44:57,391 --> 00:45:03,391
Addams Family Values is a 1993 American black comedy film, based on
the comic strip characters created by Charles Addams.

12
00:49:02,608 --> 00:49:08,608
It is the sequel to The Addams Family (1991).

13
00:53:07,826 --> 00:53:13,826
Directed by Barry Sonnenfeld and written by Paul Rudnick, the film features most of the cast members from the original film, including
Anjelica Huston, Raul Julia, Christopher Lloyd and Christina Ricci, with Joan Cusack and Carol Kane joining the cast.

14
00:57:13,043 --> 00:57:19,043
Compared to its predecessor, which retained something of the madcap approach of the 1960s
sitcom, Addams Family Values is played more for dark and macabre laughs.

15
01:01:18,260 --> 01:01:24,260
The film revolves around the family's adjustments
to the birth of new baby Pubert.

16
01:05:23,478 --> 01:05:29,478
Subplots include Uncle Fester marrying the new nanny Debbie Jellinsky, who is a serial killer intending to murder
him for his inheritance; and teenagers Wednesday and Pugsley Addams being sent to summer camp.

17
01:09:28,695 --> 01:09:34,695
Addams Family Values was released in the United States on
November 19, 1993, by Paramount Pictures.

18
01:13:33,913 --> 01:13:39,913
In contrast to its predecessor's mixed reception, the film was well received by critics but it was not as
financially successful, with a box office gross of $111 million against a budget of $47 million.

19
01:17:39,130 --> 01:17:45,130
In the decades since its release, the film has become
acclaimed for its humor and performances.

20
01:21:44,347 --> 01:21:50,347
The film was followed by a further sequel, Addams Family Reunion.

21
01:25:49,565 --> 01:25:55,565
The film explores themes of dancing, jealousy, baby,
sibling relationship, summer camp.

22
01:29:54,782 --> 01:30:00,782
The tone is lighthearted.
